{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/787476-sell-me-on-mage-sorcerer-s-crusade","id":787476,"title":"Sell me on Mage: Sorcerer's Crusade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-16T10:22:35-08:00","id":787476,"title":"Sell me on Mage: Sorcerer's Crusade","content":"Never really played any of the Dark Age (or similar Era supplements) for the CWoD and since Mage is my preferred game line I thought I'd pick it up sometime. Before I make that decision, however, I'd like a little input from the community on the finer points of this version of Mage and how it differs from Mage the Ascension (beyond the fact that they are two very different points in time)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10287-drnevermore","name":"DrNevermore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10287_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T03:07:15-08:00","id":788642,"title":"","content":"Sorcerors Crusade is a game I'm currently running, and one I enjoy quite a bit. It runs on the same basic principles as Ascension as far as magic goes, but in general it's more lenient with what is casual and vain (coincidental and vulgar). Paradox is... differrent. It's called the Scourge and it can equally help or harm you, and it is personalized in a brilliant series of quirky personages known as Scourgelings who your characters get to engage with. The Scourge resonates with the characters intents and situation for the most dramatic effects possible.<br /> <br /> There is a lot of familiarity with old faces presented in a different time... and a lot of factions who are completely different because they are nowhere close to what they are in the modern day. The Order of Reason is especially different, and the groups within will be familiar but drastically different. For instance, they are not even actively antagonistic to the Traditions when they are not meddling in their own projects. They can even be allies at times! The Council of Traditions have just gathered for the first time, and an era of great exploration and discovery has started.<br /> <br /> Now add marauding Nephandic armies, tradition politics painted by the fact that most of them hated each others guts before joining up, skyships, the New World, ancient empires all over the world and the excesses and glories of the Renessiance, and you have Sorcerors Crusade.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages Mage is a whole different game than Sorceror's Crusade - it's a about insular magical societies with highly defined magical practices whose mechanics rely on their magical philosophies, rather than a purple paradigm. I suggest taking a look, but it's a much bigger bite than Sorcerors Crusade.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T10:18:57-08:00","id":789811,"title":"","content":"I am suddenly compelled to buy this book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10287-drnevermore","name":"DrNevermore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10287_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":